---
import BinaryBackground from "@/components/BinaryBackground.astro";
---

<section id="hero" class="relative z-0 max-w-6xl mx-auto flex flex-col justify-center">
  <div class="relative min-h-screen p-6 pb-(--nav-height) flex flex-col md:flex-row-reverse items-end justify-end md:justify-between gap-2 md:gap-4 py-4">
    <BinaryBackground className="pb-90" />
    <BinaryBackground />

    <ul class="stats space-y-5 ml-auto md:ml-0 self-center">
      <li>
        <p>Experience</p>
        <h2>4+<span class="text-xl">yrs</span></h2>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Applications</p>
        <h2>3+</h2>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Websites</p>
        <h2>10+</h2>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Repositories</p>
        <h2>40+</h2>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Open to work</p>
        <h2>Yes</h2>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div
      id="hero-intro"
      class="w-full grow flex flex-col justify-between min-h-[60vh] md:min-h-[75vh] mb-5"
    >
      <div class="grow flex flex-col justify-center py-12">
        <div class="hero-ctas flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between sm:items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4 py-2 pb-4 max-w-lg">
          <p class="text-sm font-montserrat text-muted font-semibold">
            Facing architectural bottlenecks or scaling challenges? 
            <a href="/inquiry" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-iceberg font-bold text-primary hover:underline ml-1">
              Submit a Scoping Inquiry →
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3 mt-auto">
        <!--<h1 class="hero-title text-4xl font-bold font-iceberg text-primary flex gap-6 py-2">-->
        <!--  Isaac.-->
        <!--</h1>-->
        <p
          class="hero-text max-w-lg text-sm text-muted font-montserrat font-semibold overflow-hidden leading-relaxed"
        >
          <span class="block">
            Understand the machine before abstracting over it.
          </span>
          <span class="block text-foreground mt-2">
            Every abstraction must earn its cost; complexity is a deliberate
            trade-off.
          </span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul
    id="about"
    class="min-h-[150dvh] p-4 space-y-20 mt-4 pt-32 text-lg text-foreground grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 grid-rows-3 gap-5 justify-between overflow-hidden"
  >
    <li
      id="me"
      class="identity row-start-1 md:col-start-2 md:ml-0 self-center py-2"
    >
      <h2
        class="py-2 font-iceberg font-bold text-primary text-3xl border-b border-neutral-900 mb-4"
      >
        Who I Am
      </h2>

      <div class="leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-muted">
        <p>
          My name is <span class="font-iceberg text-primary">Isaac</span>. I’m a software engineer and system architect who builds reliable
          infrastructure for organizations where correctness, security, and
          long-term maintainability are non-negotiable.
        </p>
        <p>
          I specialize in evolving backend-heavy platforms that handle
          sensitive data, complex workflows, and real operational constraints.
          My work spans greenfield builds to legacy modernization, always
          focusing on software that survives production, not just the demo.
        </p>
        <p>
          I don’t chase hype. I design architectures that are understandable,
          auditable, and resilient—solutions that teams can maintain and
          businesses can trust.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li
      id="build"
      class="identity md:col-start-1 row-start-2 self-center py-2"
    >
      <h2
        class="py-2 font-iceberg font-bold text-primary text-3xl border-b border-neutral-900 mb-4"
      >
        Technical Expertise
      </h2>

      <div class="max-w-xl leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <p class="text-muted">
          I architect, build, and modernize software systems with a relentless
          focus on backend stability and data integrity.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h6 class="text-primary font-iceberg font-semibold">
            This includes:
          </h6>
          <ul
            class="list-disc list-outside text-muted text-base space-y-4 pl-4"
          >
            <li>
              <span
                class="font-montserrat font-semibold text-foreground text-sm"
                >Resilient Backend Infrastructure:
              </span>
              <span
                >Designing APIs, transactional workflows, and data-intensive
                platforms that prioritize uptime.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <span
                class="font-montserrat font-semibold text-foreground text-sm"
                >Financial Engineering:
              </span>
              <span
                >Building payment integrations and ledgers where correctness
                and idempotency are non-negotiable.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <span
                class="font-montserrat font-semibold text-foreground text-sm"
                >Legacy Modernization:
              </span>
              <span
                >Migrating critical platforms to modern stacks incrementally,
                ensuring zero downtime for production users.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <span
                class="font-montserrat font-semibold text-foreground text-sm"
                >Architecture Consulting:
              </span>
              <span
                >Helping teams untangle technical debt and make sustainable,
                long-term engineering decisions.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <span
                class="font-montserrat font-semibold text-foreground text-sm"
                >Hybrid Architectures:
              </span>
              <span
                >Balancing performance and delivery speed using BFFs (Backend
                for Frontend), serverless, and traditional monolithic
                patterns.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="text-muted">
          I translate complex business requirements into technical systems
          that scale with both usage and organizational growth.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li id="why" class="identity md:col-start-2 row-start-3 self-center py-2">
      <h2
        class="py-2 font-iceberg font-bold text-primary text-3xl border-b border-neutral-900 mb-4"
      >
        Why I Do It
      </h2>

      <div class="max-w-xl leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-muted">
        <p>
          Most costly software failures don’t stem from bad ideas — they stem
          from fragile systems, rushed architecture, and unmanaged technical
          debt.
        </p>
        <p>
          I build software because I value
          <span class="text-foreground font-semibold">resilience</span>. I
          design systems that hold up under pressure: when traffic spikes,
          when money is on the line, and long after the original authors have
          moved on.
        </p>
        <p>
          I thrive on the hard parts of engineering —state management,
          concurrency, and data integrity —because getting these right early
          saves clients years of pain, expensive rewrites, and lost trust.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
